---
title: How to Use the Backlog Tab
sidebar:
  order: 11
---
**The Backlog tab holds work that hasn't started yet, kept off the board as a single ranked list. Add ideas straight into it, reorder them by priority, and start them onto the board when the team has room.**

### **What Is the Backlog?**

Every project has one hidden Backlog stage that the board itself never shows. The Backlog tab gives that stage a dedicated, ranked view — a flat list ordered top to bottom, instead of a column of cards. Tasks keep everything (description, priority, labels, assignees, comments, files, estimate) while they sit here; they only lose their place on the board.

This tab is **internal-only** — planners and team members see it, clients never do. A client's own submitted item still shows up for them under **My requests** once it's accepted, even if staff choose to keep it in the backlog rather than starting it right away.

### **Navigation**

1. **Go to the Main Menu and select Projects.**
1. **Open the project you want to work in.**
1. **Click the Backlog tab.** A badge on the tab shows how many items are waiting.

### **Adding an Item**

Use the **quick-add row** at the top of the list: pick a type, type a title, optionally set a priority, then click **Add** (or press Enter). The item lands at the bottom of the backlog and the row stays focused so you can keep adding the next one. Quick-add is hidden if your role can't create tasks in this project.

You can also send an existing task into the backlog from:
- Its card menu on the board, or its detail view's menu — **Send to backlog**.
- Dragging a card from any board column onto the **Drop to send to backlog** zone that appears at the edge of the board while you're dragging.

A resolved task can't be sent to the backlog — resolve/reopen it first. Sending a task to the backlog keeps its assignees; it doesn't unassign anyone.

### **Reordering**

- **Drag** a row (desktop) using its handle to move it anywhere in the list.
- **Row menu** — Move up, Move down, Move to top, Move to bottom.
- **On mobile**, there's no drag handle; use the same Move up/down/top/bottom options from the row's overflow menu instead.
- **Keyboard**: `j`/`k` move focus between rows, `Shift+↑`/`Shift+↓` swap the focused row with its neighbor, `t`/`b` jump it straight to the top/bottom, `s` opens Start for the focused row, `o` opens it, `x` toggles its selection, `n` jumps to quick-add, and `?` shows the shortcut list.

Reordering (drag, the row menu's Move up/down, and the keyboard swap shortcuts) is turned off while a search, a filter, or any sort other than **Rank** is active — sorting or filtering changes what "the next row" even means, so Taskip disables reordering rather than risk placing an item next to the wrong neighbor. Move to top/bottom keep working regardless, since they don't depend on neighbors.

### **Starting an Item**

Click **Start** on a row (or select several rows and use **Start selected** from the bulk bar) to move it out of the backlog and onto the board. The Start popover lets you set:
- **Stage** — defaults to the project's first To Do stage.
- **Assignees** — optional, added on top of whoever was already assigned.
- **Priority** — leave as **Unchanged** or set a new one.
- **Estimate** — free text like "2h 30m".

### **Filtering, Searching, and Sorting**

The toolbar has a search box, filters for **Type**, **Priority**, **Assignee**, and **Label**, and a **Sort** control (Rank, Priority, Newest, Estimate). A summary line shows the item count and total estimated hours for whatever's currently filtered.

### **Working in Bulk**

Select rows with their checkboxes to open the bulk bar:
- **Select all** / **Deselect all**
- **Start selected**
- **Move to stage** — moves the selected items directly onto the board without opening the Start popover.
- **Set priority**
- **Set type**
- **Delete**

Any action you don't have permission for on a particular row is skipped automatically, with a toast telling you how many of the selected items were actually updated.

